# pixie netboot-pc live env: pin a BROAD in-tree driver set in the
# initramfs, explicitly.
#
# The live env's first action after the kernel hands off is to fetch
# its squashfs over HTTP from the kernel cmdline `fetch=` param (Debian
# live-boot), so the target's NIC must be driven from INSIDE the
# initramfs, before pivot-root -- iPXE loaded vmlinuz+initrd over the
# firmware's network stack, but from Linux on it's the kernel module
# that matters.
#
# NOTE: the Debian live-build base ALREADY defaults to MODULES=most, so
# this line is a belt-and-suspenders pin, NOT a behaviour change -- it
# guards against a future base whose default is `dep`. It does NOT, on
# its own, fix an arbitrary NIC: `most` only covers IN-TREE drivers.
# The out-of-tree DKMS driver an RTL8125 (2.5GbE) needs -- e.g. ASRock
# Rack matx -- is force-added by name in the r8125 DKMS hook
# (hooks/normal/0600-pixie-r8125-dkms.hook.chroot); `most` never pulls
# it in. See that hook for the real 2.5GbE story.
MODULES=most
